{"about":"fab3fe93125ba81777325fc75a4b1873217880cd612e89c5f659b2b669bb771b","body":"The assertion that accepting a preference for corroborated theories collapses Popper's critical rationalism into Bayesianism ignores the fundamental distinction in how 'support' is conceptualized. For Bayesians, corroboration increases the logical probability of a theory; for Popper, corroboration is a report of past performance that does not increase probability (which he argues remains zero for universal laws). One can rationally choose the theory that has survived rigorous testing without assigning it a higher probability of truth, thus maintaining the non-inductive core of his philosophy.","kind":"mini.criticism.v1","named":"False equivalence with Bayesianism"}